Description: Reject over-wide IPv4 octets in allowed_hosts before int overflow
 add_ipv4_to_acl() accumulates octet digits into a signed int with no
 per-octet digit bound. An entry like "4294967297.2.3.4" overflows int
 mid-accumulation and wraps to "1", so the ACL silently stores a
 different address than configured (e.g. becomes 1.2.3.4/32). Reject
 as soon as the accumulated value exceeds 255 - identical outcome for
 valid input, but invalid input can no longer wrap into range.
Author: GreenSEC (packaging hardening)
Origin: vendor
Bug: https://github.com/greensec/nagios-nrpe-server-ap
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
